a  of allowing emergency use to facilitate  the availability of chloroquine during  the pandemic  to treat patients for whom a clinical  trial is not available or participation  is not feasible so making clear that  we're not approving the drug for  chloroquine we're approving the drug for  discretionary emergency use when the  patient can't participate in a clinical  trial it goes on to say having concluded  that the criteria for issuance of this  authorization is met I am authorizing  the emergency use as described in the  scope of authorization for treatment of  coronavirus when clinical trials are not  available or participation is not  feasible so we are waiting on results  from what are called randomized clinical  randomized controlled trials what we  have so far as a number of small trials  have shown is conflicting information we  have some small sample sizes that say  the chloroquine treatment has worked  well we have other small samples that  say you know the people who didn't get  it did just as well as the people who  did and as Anthony Fauci has pointed out  you have to be comparing the new  treatment to some standard of care and  you need to be randomizing it just  because we've found some small studies  with a Korell correlation does not mean  that we have found a causal link and  case in point when you see just as many  studies that say the control group did  just as well you have to question the  value of this as a therapeutic treatment  we need a large properly done randomized  controlled trial until we get that we  won't really know so the FDA I believe  is doing the right thing here it seems  that the side effects and the risks are  reasonable assuming that you're getting  an EKG of patients that you're going to  give this treatment to chloroquine can  effect what's called the QT QTc interval  it's a heart related thing the FDA says  in limited situations it can be tried  when you can't get access to a clinical  trial doing the EKG is a very important  thing it's a constant balance of risk  reward side effects and the impact of  not trying it when things start to get  very very dire meanwhile there are also  people who are  taking chloroquine for the actual  approved uses who are now having trouble  getting it because many countries are  starting to stockpile chloroquine that's  another issue which we'll talk about at  another time but everything has a cost  is the point let's take a quick break  much more coming up right after this
 

